    "created_at": "2022-11-10T01:38:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2022-11-10T01:39:18Z",
    "body": "The problem is calling `screen.orientation.lock(x)` can potentially trigger an orientation change. \r\n\r\nSo, if you have a PWA that is presented in full screen via web manifest (not via `.requestFullscreen()`), the user agent can't distinguish between a user-initiated orientation change and a screen orientation API initiated orientation change. \r\n\r\n(I know you are not proposing this, but) making such events not trusted wouldn't be right, as they are user agent generated events. \r\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/1309650759/reactions",
      "total_count": 1,
      "+1": 1,
      "-1": 0,
